        "severity": "warning",
        "message": "python3 -m py_compile src/**/*.py — shell glob expansion passes the full file list as arguments, which works but is fragile; if the glob expands to nothing (no .py files found), the literal string 'src/**/*.py' is passed and py_compile will fail. Use find or a subshell: python3 -m py_compile $(find src/ -name '*.py')."
      },
      {
        "line": 111,
        "severity": "info",
        "message": "deploy step runs scripts/deploy.py but does not set PYTHONPATH=src or use a virtualenv, unlike other steps (lines 46, 64). If deploy.py has imports relying on PYTHONPATH, it may fail."
      },
      {
        "line": 18,
        "severity": "warning",
        "message": "coordinator step runs 'python3 scripts/coordinator.py parse' with no PYTHONPATH set and no dependency on the setup-python step, so it runs in the system Python. If the script requires dependencies from pyproject.toml, it will fail."
      }
    ],
    "summary": "The most critical problem is that the code-review job is disabled (if: false) but quality-check and build depend on it, silently bypassing all linting/type-checking. Additionally, the integration-test DATABASE_URL credentials may not match the docker-compose.test.yml service credentials, and the coordinator step runs without proper Python environment setup."
  },
  {
    "filename": ".github/workflows/pipeline-code-review.yml",
    "issues": [
      {
        "line": 5,
        "severity": "warning",
        "message": "branches: ['*'] triggers this workflow on pushes to every branch, including master and develop, as well as all feature/fix branches. This creates noise and unnecessary runs. Should be restricted to a specific branch pattern (e.g., master, develop, or a regex for PR branches) or triggered only on pull_request events where it is most useful."
      },
