        "severity": "warning",
        "message": "SM_TOKEN uses secrets.COMMIT_GITHUB_TOKEN || github.token, but the secret name 'COMMIT_GITHUB_TOKEN' may not be set in the repository. This silently falls back to github.token, which has the repo's read/write permissions but may lack the intended fine-grained access for pushing to yihua-zhuo/agent-job-shared-memory."
      },
      {
        "line": 40,
        "severity": "info",
        "message": "The shared-memory repository (yihua-zhuo/agent-job-shared-memory) is an external dependency cloned at runtime. If the repo is private, deleted, or the branch does not exist, the workflow will fail. There is no setup step to initialize the shared-memory directory structure (e.g., mkdir -p shared-memory/results) before cloning."
      },
      {
        "line": 68,
        "severity": "warning",
        "message": "Push shared-memory step runs 'git pull --rebase' with '2>/dev/null || true' suppressing all errors. If the rebase fails for any reason (e.g., diverged history, force-push protection), this is silently ignored and the subsequent 'git add -A && git commit' may create an unexpected commit structure or commit nothing."
      },
      {
        "line": 73,
        "severity": "warning",
        "message": "The 'git pull --rebase' combined with '|| true' means conflicts during rebase are silently swallowed. A failed rebase leaves the repo in a conflicted state, but the workflow continues and may push a broken or partial state to the shared-memory repo."
      },
      {
        "line": 77,
        "severity": "info",
        "message": "git diff --cached --quiet && exit 0 — when there are no changes to commit, the step exits early with success. The subsequent git push is correctly skipped, but this is a silent no-op rather than a logged info message."
      },
      {
        "line": 91,
        "severity": "info",
        "message": "create_cr_issue step always runs (no 'if' condition), so it will attempt to create a GitHub issue even if the code review found no critical issues or the review failed entirely. This may create noisy/no-op issues."
      }
    ],
    "summary": "This workflow triggers on every branch push (branches: ['*']), creating excessive noise. The shared-memory push silently ignores rebase failures, which could corrupt the remote repo state. No guard prevents creating GitHub issues for empty or failed reviews."
  },
  {
    "filename": ".gitignore",
    "issues": [
      {
        "line": 23,
        "severity": "info",
        "message": "The file is missing common Python gitignore entries: '*.log' for log files, '.mypy_cache/' for mypy cache, '.ruff_cache/' for ruff cache, 'tests/.pytest_cache/' (pytest cache is covered but per-test-type caches may differ), and '*.so' / '*.dylib' for compiled extensions."
      },
      {
        "line": 0,
        "severity": "info",
        "message": "No .env.example file is tracked in the repo. Without a template, new developers cannot know which environment variables are required. CLAUDE.md mentions .env is required for DATABASE_URL but there is no .env.example to guide setup."
      },
      {
        "line": 16,
        "severity": "info",
        "message": "'.idea' ignores the entire .idea directory, which is appropriate for JetBrains IDEs, but it also ignores workspace.xml and tasks.xml which may contain user-specific task state. Consider '*.icns' (macOS icon cache) for completeness."
      }
    ],
    "summary": "The gitignore covers the essentials well but is missing some common entries (mypy_cache, ruff_cache, *.log) and notably lacks a .env.example, making local setup harder for new contributors."
  },
  {
    "filename": "pytest.ini",
    "issues": [
      {
        "line": 7,
        "severity": "warning",
        "message": "addopts includes --strict-markers, which will cause pytest to fail if any test uses an unregistered marker. The 'scripts/test' directory in testpaths (line 2) may contain test files that use markers not defined in this ini (e.g., custom markers added directly in test files without being declared in the [pytest] markers section), causing CI failures."
      },
      {
        "line": 2,
        "severity": "warning",
        "message": "testpaths includes 'scripts/test' — if this directory does not exist or has no test_*.py files, pytest will emit a warning. Also, tests under scripts/test are likely informal/manual scripts rather than unit/integration tests, mixing concerns with the formal test suites."
      },
      {
        "line": 7,
        "severity": "info",
        "message": "asyncio_mode = auto is set, but if any async test uses pytest.raises() with an async function that doesn't properly await, it may produce confusing error messages. Ensure all test files under tests/ are using 'await' correctly with the auto mode."
      }
    ],
    "summary": "The --strict-markers setting combined with 'scripts/test' in testpaths creates a risk of test failures from unregistered markers. The scripts/test inclusion is unusual and should be verified to exist and not pollute the test suite."
  }
